  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 347 AM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nDeep troughing will cross southern Canada which will flatten mid-\nlevel flow for the Central Plains. High pressure aloft will park \nacross the lower Mississippi Valley with much warmer temperatures \nfocused across this area. In a post-frontal regime, surface high \npressure will settle south into western Nebraska towards mid-week. \nThis should favor slightly cooler temperatures with decreasing \nprecipitation potential. Upper ridging should develop across the \nWest Coast and return the area to more northwesterly flow before the \nnext disturbance dives southeast out of the Northwest Territories. \nThis will shunt the greatest height anomalies further south and \npromote even cooler temperatures for the end of the week into early \nnext week. Heights will continue to fall as a more pronounced \nshortwave trough takes shape over the Pacific Northwest sometime \nover the following weekend. This feature will cross the Rockies and \napproach the local area sometime towards the end of the forecast \nperiod and should support increasing precipitation chances.",
